Built stdlib-only compress.py with both requested CLI modes. It uses reversible mixed-radix packing for structured text and a bzip2 fallback; decompression needs only the compressed file. Verified byte-identical restoration of corpus_hard.txt and 29 additional test cases. The registered assay reports 62.104954% size reduction: 44,267 bytes compressed to 16,775 bytes, beating default zlib’s 22,390 bytes. The packing implementation was adopted through scored variants.